# Code quality

## Comments (English only)

- Comments in English, only where code is not self-explanatory (non-trivial logic, business rule, API constraint).
- No obvious comments (`// import`, `// call function`).
- Do not leave “changed here” notes in code — that belongs in the PR/commit.
- TODOs only with a ticket: `// TODO [ISSUE-ID]: short description`. No ticket → fix now or open a ticket first.

## Cleanliness

- Do not commit `console.log`, debug leftovers, commented-out “for later” code, unused imports/variables.
- Do not duplicate logic: before adding a hook / util / component, check `src/hooks/`, `src/utils/`, `src/components/` and reuse.

## Tests

- When adding tests, match neighboring style (matchers, mocks, `describe`/`it`).
- Place `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` next to the code under test. Do not introduce `__tests__/` folders unless that area already uses them.

## AI agent artifacts

- Agent scratch files only under `ailocal/` at the repo root (drafts, logs, dumps, plans, notes, experimental scripts).
- Do not scatter temp files under `src/` or other working dirs. `ailocal/` is gitignored and must not be committed.

## README

- When a feature needs setup (secret, cert, env var, external tool, MCP server, etc.), document it in `README.md`. Project setup lives only there.
